{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the word על regarding the women.</b> Like עם the women, as in על לחם הבכורים תנופה (Leviticus 23:20), and many are like this:" "<b>Every willing-hearted person.</b> Or: willing-heartedness, the construct state of which is not complete, like יעלה השפן (Leviticus 11:5) and ארנבת (Leviticus 11:6); and like שור שה כשבים (Deuteronomy 14:4), where each noun stands in apposition. n: The Hebrew here is terse and the precise grammatical argument compressed; the comparison to שפן / ארנבת and to שור שה כשבים appears to illustrate nouns used without full construct linkage." "<b>חח.</b> In the ear:" "<b>ונזם.</b> In the nose:" "<b>וטבעת.</b> On the finger:" "<b>וכומז.</b> On the arm:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:40:42.383265356Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}